{
  "type": "Collection",
  "id": "night-train-network-attributes",
  "stac_version": "1.1.0",
  "description": "The relational core of the Open Night Train Database, snapshot **2026-08** — four plain Parquet tables without geometry: `trips` (410 services with full attributes), `routes` (206), `agencies` (31 operators with URLs and booking contacts), and `calendar` (132 running-day patterns).\n\nThe schema is GTFS-flavored but hand-curated in [Back-on-Track's](https://back-on-track.eu/) collaborative database. Join keys: `trip_id` links to the [night-train-services](../night-train-services/collection.json) geometry; station-name strings link to [night-train-stations](../night-train-stations/collection.json); `service_id` links trips to calendar. Accessibility fields (`car_transport`, `bikes_allowed`, `wheelchair_accessible`) use [GTFS 1/2 semantics](https://gtfs.org/documentation/schedule/reference/#tripstxt) (1 = yes, 2 = no). Full field notes and runnable joins in the [agent guide](AGENTS.md).",
